      <activity id="a2911b74-ab8c-571f-88f7-6859ce3b152a" activityNameId="8eb58434-95cf-578a-9cca-132f7862da42" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Road wear emissions, lorry</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Road wear emissions, lorry
Calculation of non-exhaust emissions (tyre, brake and road wear emissions) are based on EMEP/EEA (2013) and values for net vehicle weights and average load factors. Net vehicle weights are taken from the EcoTransIT (2011) report whilst the average load factors are taken from the Tremove model v2.7b (2009) and EcoTransIT (2011) report. The road wear emissions are to air only. All particulates are accounted for as emissions to air and have particle sizes below 100um. Anything above this does not remain airborne over longer periods. In order to use the treatment of non-exhaust emissions in a transport dataset the quantity of emissions per tkm must be calculated. This must then be devided by the specific load factor of the transport in question.Non-exhaust emissions are considered to be linearly scalable to gross vehicle weight (GVW). For road wear emissions from lorries the specific quantity is 7E-9 kg/kg GVW*km.;
UUID: 92c36959-3136-3b24-bdf1-058ff7429972
The activity starts with the road abrasion. The activity ends with emissions of road abrasion.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Unspecified
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 41580000 kg
